ted_at":"2023-04-23T16:27:15Z","body":"> Regarding OSI status, I believe this is the same license that was recently submitted and withdrawn from the OSI license approval process, following several reactions to the effect that the license was (if even a license properly speaking) obviously not OSD-conformant: http://lists.opensource.org/pipermail/license-review_lists.opensource.org/2023-April/005369.html\n\nYes, correct, but changes were made in the meantime and it's basically different, as that was more an extension of OS licenses which I understood was inapplicable, at least in that form.\n\nI certainly wasn't aware about the licenses.ai great work and I am actually quite happy to discover that, even if I see they refer to a different kind of restrictions, at a different level. Thanks @richardfontana for highlighting it!\n\nI will close this issue then, change the references to a new acronym and submit again.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1519092689/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1519144953","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1948#issuecomment-1519144953","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1948","id":1519144953,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85ajE_5","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-04-23T20:04:36Z","updated_at":"2023-04-23T20:04:36Z","body":"Thanks @debonx.\r\n\r\nBefore resubmitting, I would encourage you again to take a close look at the [SPDX License List inclusion principles](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/blob/main/DOCS/license-inclusion-principles.md).\r\n\r\nIf your submitted license does not meet the requirements there, as determined by the SPDX legal community, then it won't be added to the [SPDX License List](https://spdx.org/licenses).\r\n\r\nIn particular, if you are drafting a brand new license that doesn't meet the Open Source Definition AND also is not in use by a _significant_ number of projects, it's highly unlikely that it will be added. If the license is going to include restrictions on use (§ 3, paragraph 3 of the text file you shared before), I highly doubt the SPDX legal community would view it as satisfying the Open Source Definition (I wouldn't view it this way, at least).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1519144953/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1519445287","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1948#issuecomment-1519445287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1948","id":1519445287,"node_id":"IC_k